# MODELS-REASK: the inline column's frames read a failed catalog again only
# past the failure's hold -- 5 s after the first failure in a row, 10 s after
# the second (`failureBackoffMs`, `beginLoad`, `model_cache_runtime.zig:40-54`,
# `:617`, `:621@481104fd`) -- where c1db9191 read it again a second after the
# read that failed began; and the column says `unable to load models` while
# that retry is on its way, the cache staying `.failed` (`:633-634`;
# `app_render_runtime.zig:752-753`). Against each binary's own clock, not the
# fake gateway's: the catalog is a body neither binary can read until the
# `models2` line, rather than an outage counted from the gateway's start
# (`modelsdown`, registry #19), and the launch read's failure is waited for on
# the screen. `modelsdelay 1500` holds every answer a second and a half, so a
# read is on its way long enough to be seen, and stamps the gateway log's
# catalog lines with when they were asked. From the launch read's failure:
# the column's first frame past 5 s reads again (6.5 s, the second failure,
# held 10 s from its answer at 8 s); a frame inside that hold (11.5 s) reads
# nothing, where c1db9191's one-second floor read the catalog back; one past
# it (21.5 s) reads it back.
models model-column-hold-bad.json
modelsdelay 1500
type /model
key Space
until shown unable to load models
snap col-first
wait 6.5
type o
wait 0.5
snap col-retry
wait 2.5
models2 models.json
wait 2
key BSpace
wait 3
snap col-held
wait 7
type o
until shown gpt-6-astra
snap col-back
gwlog
